    "body": "<p>Learn how to analyze your total conversions and revenue, including Klaviyo attributed values, via the Conversion overview dashboard. You can also review how many profiles are completing different numbers of conversions and the total revenue they represent. This dashboard enables you to optimize marketing efforts and increase conversion rates by targeting specific segments based on conversion behaviors.  </p>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p><a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/17655007276059\">Advanced KDP</a> and <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/33789259613595\">Marketing Analytics</a> are not included in Klaviyo’s standard marketing application, and a subscription is required to access the associated functionality.Head to our <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115000976672\">billing guide</a> to learn about how to purchase these plans.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"h_01J5V28RGNBHR41JYAS8E8V1XK\">Before you begin</h2>\n<p>This dashboard is calculated using event data. Thus, you may see a difference in how other Klaviyo reports or dashboards calculate attributed revenue (e.g., the Home dashboard uses data based on when the message was sent).</p>\n<h2 id=\"h_01J5V0ASP9YMMC8JF6S4D44W35\">Accessing and customizing the dashboard</h2>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>It is not possible to remove or replace the cards on the Conversion overview dashboard.</p>\n</div>\n<ol>\n<li>If you are an Advanced KDP customer, navigate to<strong> Advanced KDP &gt; Intelligence &gt; Customer insights &gt; Conversion overview</strong>. Alternatively, if you are a Marketing Analytics customer, navigate to <strong>Marketing Analytics &gt; Customer insights &gt; Conversion overview</strong>. </li>\n<li>Optional: Once inside the dashboard, select the <strong>Conversion metric</strong> dropdown to adjust the metric used to calculate the dashboard. For example, if you choose <em>Ordered Product</em>, you will see revenue and conversions related to completed purchases. Learn more about tracking <a href=\"https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005248128\">message conversion tracking.</a><br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720899163803\" alt=\"\" width=\"212\" height=\"374\">\n</li>\n<li>Click on the time perioddropdown. Choose from the following options:<br>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<em>Last 30 days</em> (default option)</li>\n<li><em>Last 90 days</em></li>\n<li><em>Month-to-date</em></li>\n<li><em>Year-to-date</em></li>\n<li><em>Last month</em></li>\n<li><em>Last 3 months</em></li>\n<li><em>Last 12 months</em></li>\n<li><em>Year-to-date</em></li>\n<li>\n<em>Custom</em><br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Optional: if you want to narrow your dashboard to show data specific to a certain segment, click on the <strong>Segment</strong> dropdown. From here, choose the segment you want to evaluate.<br>\nNote that if your time period is before June 21, 2023, you cannot choose a specific segment. Additionally, if you analyze all active profiles and not a specific segment, it will pull in all profiles that were active within your chosen time period. <br>\n\n<img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/29371447177499\" alt=\"segment dropdown.jpg\" width=\"286\" height=\"236\">\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>Conversions are based on segment membership at the time the conversation event occurred. </p>\n<p>For example, say you have a segment of profiles that have never placed an order. When a profile places their first order, they will exit the segment. However, since the profile was in the non-purchasers segment at the time they placed their order, the revenue is attributed to the original segment at the time of the purchase (i.e., profiles that have never placed an order).</p>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>Optional: to change the comparison period, select the <strong>Previous period</strong> dropdown.<br>\n<br>\nChoose whether you want to compare your performance in your date range to the:Reviewing the dashboard<em>Overview</em> cardThe top <em>Overview </em>card displays information on total revenue and conversions, highlighting the specific amounts that can be attributed to Klaviyo. You can see the representation of the total conversion and revenue values in both numbers and bar charts, as shown below. You will also be able to see the percentage change compared to the previous period for all revenue or conversions. A positive change will reflect as green, while a negative change will reflect as red.On the right-hand side of the card, you can review profile information associated with your conversions and revenue. These include the following values:<em>Conversion group characteristics </em>cardThe <em>Conversion group characteristics</em> card represents the total number of conversions and the revenue per grouping. The top of the card shows the conversion group (e.g., 3 conversions) and the total number of individual profiles who are in that grouping or completed a conversion event (i.e., the metric you chose at the top).The table on the bottom shows the conversion group and specific related values. For example, if you have a group of profiles who made 2 conversions, you can see what this represents in terms of the total:The <em>Total conversions</em> and <em>Total revenue</em> columns also break out these values in terms of total vs. Klaviyo attributed numbers. </li>\n</ol>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720904446875\" alt=\"time period.jpg\" width=\"468\" height=\"292\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720899160091\" alt=\"conv chart final.jpg\" width=\"749\" height=\"276\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720904454683\" alt=\"group characteristics card.jpg\" width=\"663\" height=\"361\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720899158427\" alt=\"\" width=\"659\" height=\"170\"></p>\n<p><img src=\"https://klaviyo.zendesk.com/hc/article_attachments/28720904445083\" alt=\"\" width=\"750\" height=\"219\"></p>\n<ul>\n<ul>\n<li><em>Previous year</em></li>\n<li>\n<em>Previous period</em><br>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>This option compares your data to the same prior date range. For example, if you select the <em>Previous year</em> option and set your time period to the Last 30 days, the dashboard will compare your data to the corresponding 30 days from the previous year. If you choose the <em>Previous period</em>, your data will compare to the same prior date range or, in this case, the preceding 30 days to our chosen data range.</p>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<em>Custom</em> set of date ranges.<br>\n<div class=\"bs-callout bs-callout-default\">\n<p>If you choose a custom range, your data will compare to that particular range only.</p>\n</div>\n</li>\n<li>Attributed revenue is revenue that can be directly tied to Klaviyo.</li>\n<li>Total revenue represents Klaviyo revenue and any additional revenue sources you may have (e.g., ads, other channels, in-store purchases, etc.).</li>\n<li>\n<em><strong>Active profiles</strong></em><br>\nThe total number of profiles that can be emailed through Klaviyo during your chosen time period. </li>\n<li>\n<em><strong>Profiles converted</strong></em><br>\nThe number of profiles that converted within your chosen time period.</li>\n<li>\n<em><strong>Average order value</strong></em><br>\nThe average revenue spent per conversion.</li>\n<li>Number of profiles</li>\n<li>Number of individual conversions</li>\n<li>Revenue</li>\n</ul>\n</ul>",
